<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Süleyman Askerî</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Süleyman Askeri Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Süleyman Askerî was an Ottoman officer of the Special Organisation. In 1913, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a>, he led the irregular forces that set up the Provisional Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-thrace">Western Thrace</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komotini">Gümülcine</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. He committed suicide in 1915 after defeat by the British in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suleyman-askeri.jpg" alt="Süleyman Askerî" width="200" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suleyman_Askeri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
